 "text": "Home\n/\nGovernment\n/\n Departments\n/\n Library and Community Services\n/\n Recreation and sports\n/\nGymnastics\nGymnastics\nPlease note the following upcoming closures:\nThe City of Menlo Park's Library and Community Services facilities will be closed on Wednesday, Nov. 11, for Veterans Day. We will resume our regularly held business hours the following day. \nThe City of Menlo Park’s popular gymnastics program offers youth gymnastics classes at the Arrillaga Family Gymnastics Center. Classes include Kindergym and KinderStars, where caregivers and children participate together; NewStars, MiniStars, and SuperStars for independent participation of children ages 3-6; and Level A, Level B, and Level C class progressions for children aged 6 and up.  We also offer a variety of silks, trapeze, and aerial programs, a Stretch and Strength program, and an Exploration Through Movement class.\nView and enroll in classes\nCheck out our new online registration system, which makes it easy to find and register for Menlo Park classes and events, track payments, and track family activity schedules. Mobile-friendly on your phone, laptop, or tablet. \nGymnastics\n(JPEG, 441KB)\nOpen image in slideshow\nGymnastics complex\n(JPEG, 339KB)\nOpen image in slideshow\nGymnastics complex\n(JPEG, 513KB)\nOpen image in slideshow\nFrequently asked questions\nMy child is not enjoying the class - what can I do?\nWe are happy to withdraw your child from the class. We ask that your withdraw request be made by the second class meeting. This allows us to manage classes for the entire community. \nDo you offer trial classes?\nMenlo Park Gymnastics does not offer trial classes. You may register for a class and if you do not like the class after your first session we are happy to offer you a refund or credit for the session.\nAre make-up classes available?\nMenlo Park Gymnastics does not offer make-up classes.\nCan my child be enrolled for a class where they do not meet the age requirement (due to ability or due to a desire to have my child participate with another student)?\nMenlo Park Gymnastics classes are based on age because of the physical and social development of the students. All students under 6 years old are grouped by student age. 6 year old students begin in the Level A class and are moved to higher level classes based on their ability to perform gymnastic skills on the apparatus.\nMy friends and I would like to schedule a private lesson for our group of children\nMenlo Park Gymnastics does not currently offer private gymnastics classes.\nMay I pay for and attend just a single class?\nMenlo Park Gymnastics only offers classes by session. Single classes are not currently available.\nDo you offer birthday parties?\nMenlo Park Gymnastics is unable to offer birthday party rentals at this time.\nMay I rent out the gymnastics facility?\nThe only areas currently available for rent in the gymnastics facility are the meeting rooms. Speak to a staff member if you need assistance renting a meeting room space.\nDo you have open gym times when my children and I can just play in the gym?\nMenlo Park Gymnastics does not offer an open gym time.\nContact us\nGymnastics inquiries:\nEmail us at \nRegistration@menlopark.gov\n if you need additional help or call 650-330-2224.\nArrillaga Family Gymnastics Center\n501 Laurel St.\n650-330-2224\nSuggestions or general feedback:\nWeb:           \nmenlopark.gov/feedback\nPhone:        \n650-330-2224\nTechnical support:\nEmail:         \nregistration@menlopark.gov\nShare\nFacebook\nX\nEmail\nPrint\nLinkedIn\nBack to top",
